WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:09.225
Nell: We had permission to take one thing. Kit brought a saw. I brought the little blue bowl.

2
00:00:11.475 --> 00:00:15.625
Kit: Count from the chimney. Four rows east.

3
00:00:16.225 --> 00:00:20.450
Nell: You can put that map away. I know where I fell out of a tree.

4
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:30.225
Nell: Under the boat it was still autumn. Leaves caught flat against the wire. A wasp inside a pear, perfectly still.

5
00:00:33.275 --> 00:00:36.700
Kit: Two tugs if you want me to pull.

6
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:43.900
Nell: I went down with the saw between my knees. The brass plate was exactly where we'd left it.

7
00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:54.225
Nell: Kit. September, four feet one. Nell. September, four feet one and a half. She'd scratched that half in herself, for me.

8
00:00:56.675 --> 00:01:03.150
Nell: I put the saw to the bark. Then something hit the back of my hand. A pear, coming up. And then another.

9
00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.950
Kit: Where's the plate?

10
00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:10.425
Nell: Still on the tree.

11
00:01:11.425 --> 00:01:14.225
Kit: You made me row six miles.

12
00:01:15.725 --> 00:01:17.375
Nell: Hold out the bowl.

13
00:01:19.525 --> 00:01:27.150
Nell: We split the last pear with her thumbnail. The flesh was salt all the way through. In the middle, six brown seeds.

14
00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:32.725
Kit: Your kitchen gets the morning sun.

15
00:01:34.325 --> 00:01:40.000
Nell: She pushed five seeds across the table. The sixth she slid into her shirt pocket.

